@startuml
title GC2D Domain Model and Simulation Lifecycle

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

class Potential {
  Field model
}

class Dynamics {
  Equations of motion
}

class "Initial configuration\n(state geometry)" as InitialConfiguration {
  Initial physical state
  State layout and geometry
}

class "Initial-value problem" as InitialValueProblem {
  Dynamics + initial configuration
}

class "Numerical method" as NumericalMethod {
  Time-integration algorithm
}

class "ExplicitEuler\n(public numerical method)" as ExplicitEuler {
  z + h f(t, z)
}

class "ABBA4Implicit1\n(public numerical method)" as ABBA4Implicit1 {
  Fourth-order Yoshida triple jump
}

class "ImplicitABBA1TangentTaylor\n(public numerical method)" as ImplicitABBA1TangentTaylor {
  z + h f + h^2 / 2 D(Psi_ABBA) f
}

class "ABBA4Implicit1TangentTaylor\n(public numerical method)" as ABBA4Implicit1TangentTaylor {
  z + h f + h^2 / 2 D(Psi_ABBA4) f
}

class "Simulation request" as SimulationRequest {
  Time span, steps, output sampling
}

class "Simulation runner" as SimulationRunner {
  Validates and executes a run
}

class "Solution\n(computed trajectory)" as Solution {
  Immutable sampled times, states, diagnostics
}

class "High-precision numerical reference\n(versioned artifact)" as NumericalReference {
  DOP853 trajectory + independent Radau audit
  Immutable arrays, validated manifest, explanation, checksum
}

class "Numerical accuracy study" as NumericalAccuracyStudy {
  Periodic distances from computed solutions
  Ten-method, focused ABBA4, or tangent-Taylor/Euler refinement
  Time series, summaries, orders, and resolution margin
}

class "ABBA4Implicit1 symplecticity study" as ABBA4SymplecticityStudy {
  Exact ideal-root local and accumulated tangents
  Arithmetic mean of individual trajectory defects
}

class "Implicit ABBA reversibility study" as ABBAReversibilityStudy {
  Independent signed reverse ABBA or ABBA4 solve at every selected endpoint
  J-minus J-plus closure and normalized increment closure
}

class "ABBA tangent-Taylor trajectory study" as ABBATangentTaylorStudy {
  Aligned original and proposed trajectories
  Minimum-image periodic drift
}

Potential --> Dynamics : defines field forces
Dynamics --> InitialValueProblem
InitialConfiguration --> InitialValueProblem
InitialValueProblem --> SimulationRunner
NumericalMethod --> SimulationRunner
NumericalMethod <|-- ExplicitEuler
NumericalMethod <|-- ABBA4Implicit1
NumericalMethod <|-- ImplicitABBA1TangentTaylor
NumericalMethod <|-- ABBA4Implicit1TangentTaylor
SimulationRequest --> SimulationRunner
SimulationRunner --> Solution : produces
Dynamics --> NumericalReference : adaptive integration of same ODE
InitialConfiguration --> NumericalReference : exact initial state
NumericalReference --> NumericalAccuracyStudy : verified reference
Solution --> NumericalAccuracyStudy : compared trajectories
ABBA4Implicit1 --> NumericalAccuracyStudy : focused nested-step study
ExplicitEuler --> NumericalAccuracyStudy : tangent-Taylor baseline
ImplicitABBA1TangentTaylor --> NumericalAccuracyStudy : nested-step comparison
ABBA4Implicit1TangentTaylor --> NumericalAccuracyStudy : nested-step comparison
ABBA4Implicit1 --> ABBA4SymplecticityStudy : exact tangent study
Solution --> ABBA4SymplecticityStudy : analyzed trajectory
NumericalMethod --> ABBAReversibilityStudy : implicit ABBA trajectory
ABBA4Implicit1 --> ABBAReversibilityStudy : three-factor tangent products
Solution --> ABBAReversibilityStudy : accepted endpoints
ImplicitABBA1TangentTaylor --> ABBATangentTaylorStudy : compared with ImplicitABBA1
ABBA4Implicit1TangentTaylor --> ABBATangentTaylorStudy : compared with ABBA4Implicit1
Solution --> ABBATangentTaylorStudy : aligned trajectory pair

note bottom of InitialConfiguration
  This role owns initial state geometry and
  component-major layout only. Physical rho
  and eta parameters belong to Dynamics.
end note

note bottom of Solution
  Solution is the read-only trajectory evolved in time.
  It is distinct from the initial-state
  geometry used to define a problem.
end note

note bottom of NumericalReference
  This is a computed float64 surrogate for the same
  interpolated ODE, not an analytical trajectory or
  physical-model validation. A field fingerprint and
  DOP853/Radau discrepancy make its scope auditable.
end note

note bottom of NumericalMethod
  The public ImplicitABBA1 method uses the reduced multiplier
  equation, while ImplicitABBA2 solves the
  equivalent simultaneous output-multiplier system.
  Both converge to the same projected physical map.
  BM4Implicit1 and BM4Implicit2 apply these two
  projection formulations around a full BM4 cycle.
  MidpointBM4 applies the uncoupled twelve-stage
  cycle and averages both copies once at its end.
  Its exact observer composes analytic stage factors,
  propagates one extended tangent per trajectory,
  projects it to a physical 2x2 Jacobian, and averages
  the resulting individual symplecticity defects.
  The common independent-trajectory observer applies the
  same local-and-accumulated measurement to MidpointABBA,
  ImplicitABBA1, ABBA4Implicit1, and BM4Implicit1. It differentiates the
  explicit shears analytically and differentiates converged
  implicit projections with the implicit-function theorem;
  BM4 first composes its twelve exact coupled stage factors.
  Reported means are arithmetic means of the individual
  2x2 physical defects, not a packed-system RMS.
  ProjectedBM4Composition instead averages and
  re-embeds both copies after every internal stage.
  Its symplecticity study differentiates all twelve
  projected stages and reports both complete-step
  and accumulated physical-map defects.
  Every implicit method selects Newton or Broyden.
  Newton evaluates the formulation-specific residual
  Jacobian; Broyden shares one residual-only secant solver
  initialized by the corresponding small-step matrix.
  Physical step Jacobians remain optional diagnostics for the original maps.
  The two tangent-Taylor methods explicitly promote the exact base-map tangent
  into z + h f + h^2 / 2 D(Psi_base) f and recompute it on their own trajectory.
  The implicit-ABBA Jacobian observer analyzes each
  local physical tangent without area or symplecticity metrics.
  The implicit-ABBA reversibility observer independently solves a signed
  reverse root from each selected accepted endpoint. It compares
  J-minus J-plus with the identity and normalizes the proposed increment
  closure by max(norm(Delta-plus), norm(Delta-minus)).
  For ABBA4 it composes J3 J2 J1 separately in both time directions.
  Its study result can evaluate the effective electric field at
  observed step endpoints and derive each finite physical increment
  Delta z[n] = z[n+1] - z[n], its norm, and its oriented
  atan2(Delta y[n], Delta x[n]) direction from accepted states.
  The implicit-ABBA iteration observer separately records
  nonlinear work, residual evaluations, and convergence metrics produced by each
  accepted step, without repeating the nonlinear solve.
  The implicit-BM4 iteration observer provides the same metrics
  for the reduced and simultaneous projection around each complete
  twelve-stage BM4 cycle.
  The four-method trajectory study uses one common physical
  problem and step, compares all six method pairs, and keeps
  per-step nonlinear work aligned with the computed solutions.
  The ten-variant trajectory study adds MidpointABBA and
  MidpointBM4, and runs each implicit ABBA/BM4 formulation
  once with Newton and once with Broyden. All variants share
  one initial configuration and saved-time grid; the result
  reports 45 periodic-distance pairs, ten runtimes, and eight
  aligned nonlinear-work series.
  The accuracy study validates a versioned DOP853 reference
  against an independent Radau solve, then measures all ten
  fixed-step trajectories with periodic minimum-image distances.
  It reports particle-RMS evolution, final and maximum error,
  the margin above the reference discrepancy, and runtime.
  Its step-refinement runner uses nested complete steps and one
  common saved cadence aligned with every main grid; error gains
  and observed orders therefore require neither interpolation
  nor off-grid shadow steps.
end note

note bottom of ABBA4Implicit1
  One step composes three complete reduced projected
  ImplicitABBA1 roots with Yoshida coefficients
  gamma = 1 / (2 - 2^(1/3)) and
  delta = -2^(1/3) / (2 - 2^(1/3)).
  The signed intervals are gamma h, delta h, gamma h;
  the middle solve runs backward, and every solve owns
  a separate projection multiplier. The exact physical
  tangent is composed in flow order as J3 @ J2 @ J1.
end note

note top of Potential
  Public APIs are grouped by responsibility in
  potential, dynamics, initial_conditions,
  simulation, diagnostics, studies, and visualization.
end note

legend bottom
  |= Concept |= Responsibility |
  | Potential | Physical field model |
  | Dynamics | Equations induced by the field model |
  | Initial configuration | Initial state and coordinate layout |
  | Simulation | Execution using a problem, numerical method, and request |
  | Solution | Computed trajectory and diagnostics |
  | Numerical reference | Audited high-precision trajectory for the same ODE |
  | Accuracy study | Distance between computed solutions and the reference |
  | Symplecticity study | Exact local and accumulated physical-map defects |
endlegend

@enduml
